# Trailing slashes are deliberately absent from the generated- and vendored-
# content patterns below. A trailing slash makes a pattern directory-only, and a
# *symlink* is not a directory as far as git is concerned — so `node_modules/`
# ignores a real node_modules but not a symlinked one, which then shows up as an
# untracked `?? node_modules` that a `git add -A` would commit. That is not
# hypothetical here: `npm ci` needs a `read:packages` token, so the practical way
# to run the suite in a `.claude/worktrees/*` worktree is to symlink the main
# clone's installed tree. See #171, and test/gitignore-symlink.test.ts, which
# fails if a slash comes back.

node_modules
dist
*.log
.DS_Store
.env
.env.local
.context/compound-engineering/
.claude/.reclaim-session.json
dist-safari

# Store-upload zips built by `npm run package`. Reproducible from the tree at a
# given commit, so committing them would only invite uploading a stale one.
release

# Xcode and SwiftPM build output. `apple/build/` is not enough: xcodebuild puts
# its output beside the project, at `apple/GlassFrog Clipper/build/`, and
# SwiftPM puts its own under the package. Both are large and neither is source.
# The web extension bundled into the Xcode project is compiled from src/ by a
# Run Script build phase, so it is build output like dist/ and is not committed.
apple/**/Shared (Extension)/Resources/
apple/**/build/
apple/**/.build/
apple/**/xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate

# The signing team identifier, which belongs to whoever is building rather than
# to this repository. Signing.xcconfig includes it optionally, so its absence is
# a working state: builds are unsigned, exactly as CI wants them.
# See apple/GlassFrog Clipper/Configurations/Local.xcconfig.example.
apple/**/Configurations/Local*.xcconfig
!apple/**/Configurations/Local.xcconfig.example
